!Name: rake-c12d-p1536
!C A diagonal c/12 period 1536 sideways rake demonstrating period doubling.
!C This is a rake composed of a base period 96 sideways rake whose output
!C passes through four copies of a period doubling Cordership convoy.
!C Period doubling works by having forward gliders change the manner in
!C which beehives produced by two adjacent Corderships are destroyed.
!C In one mode, each of the spaceships destroys its own beehives.  In
!C the other mode, each spaceship destroys the other spaceship's beehives.
!C David I. Bell, July 2005
!Source: jslife-moving
